00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.900
cage this morning. Man, in my day, if I'd ever broken quarantine like that, they would

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:12.310
have. Son, you got rattlers in your stomach? I've been up on the shuttle before, Dad. Twice.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:21.050
Didn't matter how many times I went up. Every time, rattlers. First EVA, first time I walked

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:25.050
on the moon. I'm not going EVA, Dad. I'm not walking on the moon. I'm just running a

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:29.960
little experiment. Yeah, an experiment to prove your own theory. You have any idea how

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:36.280
proud that makes me. That's something I never did. I mean, the guys in the button-down collars and the

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:42.710
neckties, they got to use their brains. The only thing I ever got to use was the guts and the seat

